Z||000000||foxgapfiero||11-03-2001||04:20 PM||||When I swapped the 3.4 into my GT I noticed that with the engine at idle the oil pressure guage is pegged past the 80 lb mark. As the oil warms up the pressure does go down but is still beyond the 80 lb mark. Is there a fix for this or is the oil pressure in the 3.4 this high? The sending unit was new on the 2.8 and on there it read correctly for the 2.8. I thought I'd ask before putting a mechanical guage in the place of the sender and checking it that way.  <P>------------------<BR>Mark Hoagland<BR>86GT 3.4<BR>88GT T-Top<BR>85GT caddy v-8 next swap<BR>84SE trailer next project||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-03-2001||08:20 PM||||My 3.4L reads 60, using Mobil One 10-30.  Sounds like a bad oil sending unit. I've replaced the oil sending unit in my 3.4 twice this year.  Not a real good design for the oil sending unit.||||reg||1
